5. STATUTORY INTEROPERABILITY & FAIR USE NOTICE
================================================================================

Pryzma is an independent compatibility engine designed to restore visual shaderpack
and resourcepack functionality in modern Minecraft runtimes.

All compatibility interfaces, configuration parsers, and format adapters are
developed and distributed strictly for the purpose of technical interoperability,
under statutory provisions including:
- United States Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 107 - Fair Use for Interoperability;
  Sega Enterprises Ltd. v. Accolade, Inc.; Sony Computer Entertainment, Inc. v.
  Connectix Corp.);
- European Union Directive 2009/24/EC, Article 6 (Decompilation for Interoperability);
- Civil Code of the Russian Federation, Part IV, Article 1280 (Right of Legitimate
  Users to Decompile and Adapt for Interoperability).

Pryzma is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Mojang Studios,
Microsoft Corporation, or predecessor visual modification teams. All registered
trademarks belong to their respective owners.
